rule ROUTE106 "handler-exposes-internals" {
  lang python
  severity error

  find c: call where c.text ~ /jsonify\(\s*(dict\()?(os\.environ|app\.config|traceback\.format_exc\(\))/
  report c "a handler returns process environment, configuration or a traceback to the client"

  example fire python """
    return jsonify(dict(os.environ))  #~ error
  """
  example clean python """
    return jsonify({"status": "ok"})
  """
  example notapplicable markdown """
    Prose returns nothing.
  """
  explain """
    Environment variables, application config and tracebacks carry secrets, paths and library versions that help an attacker. The check reads Flask-style `jsonify(...)` calls; other frameworks and languages need an adapter and are reported Unresolved by the family, never clean.
    ## Remedy
    Return a fixed, minimal payload, log the detail server side, and answer errors with a generic message and an error id.
  """
}
